<section class="ref-group"><h2>Battles <span class="n">19</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-vincy"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-vincy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Vincy</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 717</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Vincy was fought on 21 March 717 near Cambrai, in northern France, during the civil war that followed the death of Pepin of Herstal.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-covadonga"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-covadonga.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Covadonga</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · c. 722</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Covadonga was fought in the mountains of Asturias, traditionally in 718 but more probably in 722, between a Muslim force and Asturian rebels led by the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-marj-ardabil"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-marj-ardabil.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Marj Ardabil</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 730</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Marj Ardabil was fought in December 730 near Ardabil, in north-western Iran, between a Khazar army and the forces of the Umayyad Caliphate.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-defile"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-defile.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Defile</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 731</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Defile was fought in 731 at the Takhtakaracha pass between Kesh and Samarkand in Central Asia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tours"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tours.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Tours</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 732 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Tours, also called the Battle of Poitiers, was fought in 732 CE in western France, where Frankish forces under Charles Martel defeated an Umayyad army led…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-boarn"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Boarn</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 734</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Boarn was fought in 734 on the river Boarn (Boorne) in present-day Friesland, Netherlands.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kharistan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kharistan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Kharistan</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 737</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Kharistan was fought in December 737 in Guzgan, in present-day northern Afghanistan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-qudayd"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Qudayd</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 747</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Qudayd was fought in 747 at Qudayd, between Mecca and Medina, where Ibadi Kharijite rebels from Hadramawt under Abu Hamza al-Mukhtar ibn Awf defeated an…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-great-zab"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Great Zab</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 750</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Great Zab was fought in January 750 on the Great Zab River in northern Iraq, where the forces of the Abbasid Revolution defeated the last Umayyad…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-talas"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-talas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Talas</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 751</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Talas was fought in 751 near the Talas River in Central Asia, where a Tang army was defeated by an Abbasid-allied force.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-burford"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Burford</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 752</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Burford was fought in 752 near Burford in Oxfordshire, where, according to the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle, Cuthred of Wessex defeated Æthelbald of Mercia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-musara"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Musara</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 756</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Musara was fought in May 756 on the banks of the Guadalquivir near Córdoba.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-anchialus-763"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-anchialus-763.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Anchialus (763)</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 763</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Anchialus was fought on 30 June 763 near Anchialus on the Black Sea coast.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-roncevaux-pass"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Roncevaux Pass</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 778</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Roncevaux Pass was fought in 778 in the Pyrenees, where Charlemagne's rearguard was ambushed and destroyed by Basques during the withdrawal from a failed…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bensington"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Bensington</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 779</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Bensington was fought in 779 at Bensington, now Benson in Oxfordshire, where Offa of Mercia defeated Cynewulf of Wessex and took the town.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-suntel"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-suntel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Süntel</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 782</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Süntel was fought in 782 in the Süntel hills near the Weser, in present-day Lower Saxony, when a Saxon army raised by Widukind destroyed a Frankish…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fakhkh"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Fakhkh</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · Revolt · 786</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Fakhkh was fought in June 786 near Mecca, where Abbasid forces crushed a revolt of the Alid al-Husayn ibn Ali, a descendant of Hasan ibn Ali.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-markellai"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-markellai.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Markellai</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 792</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Markellai was fought in 792 near the fortress of Markellai, close to present-day Karnobat in Bulgaria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lutos"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-lutos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Lutos</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 794</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Lutos was fought in 794 in Asturias, when Alfonso II ambushed a Muslim army of the emir Hisham I returning from a campaign that had sacked Oviedo.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Sieges <span class="n">1</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/second-arab-siege-of-constantinople"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/second-arab-siege-of-constantinople.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Second Arab siege of Constantinople</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 717–718 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Second Arab siege of Constantinople was a land and sea assault on the Byzantine capital by the Umayyad Caliphate in 717–718 CE.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Wars &amp; campaigns <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-conquest-of-hispania"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/umayyad-conquest-of-hispania.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Umayyad conquest of Hispania</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 711 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Umayyad conquest of Hispania was the Muslim conquest of most of the Iberian Peninsula beginning in 711 CE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-conquest-of-sind"><span class="enc-name">Umayyad conquest of Sind</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 711 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Umayyad conquest of Sind was the campaign of 711 CE in which forces led by Muhammad ibn Qasim conquered Sind, in the lower Indus valley in present-day Pakistan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/frankish-civil-war-715-718"><span class="enc-name">Frankish Civil War (715–718)</span><span class="enc-type">War · 715–718</span><span class="enc-snip">The Frankish Civil War of 715–718 was a struggle for power after the death of the mayor of the palace Pepin of Herstal.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-invasion-of-gaul"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/umayyad-invasion-of-gaul.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Umayyad invasion of Gaul</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 719–759</span><span class="enc-snip">The Umayyad invasion of Gaul was the series of campaigns launched from al-Andalus into Frankish territory after 719, when Narbonne was taken.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/third-fitna"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/third-fitna.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Third Fitna</span><span class="enc-type">War · 744–747</span><span class="enc-snip">The Third Fitna was a series of civil wars in the Umayyad Caliphate that began in 744 with the overthrow and killing of al-Walid II by his cousin Yazid III.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/saxon-wars"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/saxon-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Saxon Wars</span><span class="enc-type">War · 772–804</span><span class="enc-snip">The Saxon Wars were the campaigns fought from 772 to 804 by Charlemagne against the Saxons, a Germanic people living east of the Rhine.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/avar-campaign"><span class="enc-name">Avar campaign</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 791–803</span><span class="enc-snip">The Avar campaign was a series of wars waged by Charlemagne and his commanders against the Avar Khaganate in the Pannonian basin between 791 and 803.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Revolts &amp; revolutions <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/berber-revolt"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/berber-revolt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Berber Revolt</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 739–743 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Berber Revolt was a series of uprisings in North Africa between 739 and 743 CE against the rule of the Umayyad Caliphate.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-revolution"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/abbasid-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Abbasid Revolution</span><span class="enc-type">Revolution · 750</span><span class="enc-snip">The Abbasid Revolution was the uprising that overthrew the Umayyad Caliphate and brought the Abbasid dynasty to power in 750.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">An Lushan Rebellion</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 755–763</span><span class="enc-snip">The An Lushan Rebellion was a devastating revolt against the Tang Dynasty that lasted from 755 to 763.</span></a></li></ul></section>
